{"name":"King Salmon","hex":"#d88668","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"King Salmon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Bristol Bay Borough, Alaska; borough seat of Lake and Peninsula Borough.","An unincorporated community in Humboldt County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/King_Salmon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chinook salmon","blocks":[{"text":"The Chinook salmon is the largest and most valuable species of Pacific salmon. Its common name is derived from the Chinookan peoples. Other vernacular names for the species include king salmon, quinnat salmon, tsumen, spring salmon, blackmouth, and tyee salmon. The scientific species name is based on the Russian common name chavycha (чавыча)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Chinook_Salmon_Adult_Male.jpg/330px-Chinook_Salmon_Adult_Male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinook_salmon","wikidata":"Q833503"},{"title":"King Salmon (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"King Salmon: The Big Catch (キングサーモン) is a 1992 Sega Genesis/Mega Drive fishing video game that was developed by Hot-B and was released by Vic Tokai in North America. It was due for release in Europe by July, but the plan was cancelled."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a3/KingSalmonNACoverArt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Salmon_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q3197030"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"},{"title":"Salmon","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon are any of several commercially important species of ray-finned fish that can live in either freshwater or saltwater from the genera Salmo and Oncorhynchus of the family Salmonidae, native to tributaries of the North Atlantic (Salmo) and North Pacific (Oncorhynchus) basins. Salmon is a colloquial or common name used for fish in this group, but is not a scientific name. Other closely related fish in the same family include trout, char, grayling, whitefish, lenok and taimen, all coldwater fish of the subarctic and cooler temperate regions with some sporadic endorheic populations in Central Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Salmo_salar.jpg/330px-Salmo_salar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon","wikidata":"Q2796766"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/OncorhynchusTschawytscha2.jpg/500px-OncorhynchusTschawytscha2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/OncorhynchusTschawytscha2.jpg/500px-OncorhynchusTschawytscha2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A male Chinook in his spawning phase","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOncorhynchusTschawytscha2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/King_salmon_tail_by_Nick_Longrich.jpg/500px-King_salmon_tail_by_Nick_Longrich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or